# .dockerignore — repo root.
#
# The ONLY Docker build in this repo is the Fly sync worker (`workers/sync/Dockerfile`),
# and since 2026-08-08 its build context is this directory rather than `workers/sync/`.
# Reason: `workers/sync/src/reports/excel/findingsBridge.ts` imports the app's finding
# flattener across the package boundary with a real relative path, so the container has
# to contain `lib/sync/findings.ts`, `lib/sync/cases-fold.ts` and
# `app/(app)/sync/types.ts`. With the old worker-scoped context they were absent and
# `fly deploy` died at `npm run build`. See the header of workers/sync/Dockerfile.
#
# A repo-root context would otherwise upload the whole monorepo (node_modules, .next,
# .git, supabase/, fixtures — hundreds of MB) to Fly's remote builder on every deploy.
# So this file is DENY-ALL-THEN-ALLOW: `*` excludes everything, and each block below
# re-admits exactly one path. Docker applies patterns in order and the LAST match wins,
# which is why every intermediate directory is re-included and then re-emptied
# (`!lib` then `lib/*` then `!lib/sync/findings.ts`) — un-ignoring a directory without
# re-emptying it would silently ship all of its siblings.
#
# KEEP IN STEP WITH THE DOCKERFILE. Anything a COPY needs must be allowed here, or the
# file is missing in the image and the build fails only on Fly. `npm run
# verify:container-build` (in workers/sync) parses this file AND the Dockerfile, rebuilds
# the exact resulting file set in a temp dir and runs esbuild against it — that is the
# gate that turns "forgot to un-ignore it" into a red local build.
#
# NOTE: this file affects Docker builds only. Vercel (which builds the Next.js app from
# `main`) does not read it, and neither does git.

# Deny everything.
*

# ---- the worker package -------------------------------------------------------
!workers
workers/*
!workers/sync
workers/sync/*
!workers/sync/package.json
!workers/sync/package-lock.json
!workers/sync/tsconfig.json
!workers/sync/esbuild.config.mjs
!workers/sync/src
!workers/sync/src/**

# ---- the ONE worker->app crossing --------------------------------------------
# Transitive closure of workers/sync/src/reports/excel/findingsBridge.ts. FOUR files, and
# four only: findings.ts imports cases-fold + portable-hash + the contract types,
# cases-fold imports the contract types, and portable-hash and the contract types import
# nothing at all.
#
# `portable-hash.ts` joined the closure on 2026-08-19 when `findings.ts` grew the
# finding-ACK fingerprint, and this file was not updated with it — so the deploy gate was
# already red before the BUG-026 work touched anything. That is precisely the failure mode
# DEPLOY.md warns about: the app half stays green on Vercel while the worker cannot build
# at all. When the closure grows, it grows HERE and in the Dockerfile, together.
!lib
lib/*
!lib/sync
lib/sync/*
!lib/sync/findings.ts
!lib/sync/cases-fold.ts
!lib/sync/portable-hash.ts

!app
app/*
!app/(app)
app/(app)/*
!app/(app)/sync
app/(app)/sync/*
!app/(app)/sync/types.ts

# ---- belt and braces ----------------------------------------------------------
# Already covered by the deny-all above; spelled out so that a future `!`-block written
# one level too broad cannot quietly re-admit them.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
